From: Juan Sanchez <juanesf91@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] regulator: axp20x: cycle AXP318 rails across the 1.54 V threshold

The AXP318 DCDC6/7/8/9 voltage encoding is split at 1.54 V. The hardware
allows any selector to be written while the rail is off, but it must not
cross that boundary while the rail is on. axp318_threshold_check() rejects
such a transition with -EBUSY, which makes regulator registration fail when
the bootloader leaves a rail on the other side of the boundary from the DTS
constraint. On the Cubie A7A this happens to dcdc8 and aborts the whole
AXP318 regulator probe, leaving all pinctrl supplies in deferred probe.

Cycle the output off, write the requested selector, then restore the
previous state when a crossing is needed. Rails that are already off can be
programmed directly, and non-crossing transitions keep the existing path.

This keeps dcdc8 enabled and configured from the base device tree so a
future UFS driver needs no DTS change.

Signed-off-by: Juan Sanchez <juanesf91@gmail.com>
Assisted-by: OpenCode (Big Pickle) <noreply@opencode.ai>
---
diff --git a/drivers/regulator/axp20x-regulator.c b/drivers/regulator/axp20x-regulator.c
--- a/drivers/regulator/axp20x-regulator.c
+++ b/drivers/regulator/axp20x-regulator.c
@@ -658,13 +658,36 @@
 static int axp318_threshold_set_voltage_sel(struct regulator_dev *rdev,
 					    unsigned int sel)
 {
-	int ret;
+	int ret, enabled;
+
+	enabled = rdev->desc->ops->is_enabled(rdev);
+	if (enabled < 0)
+		return enabled;
+
+	/* The AXP318 allows any voltage while the rail is off, but not crossing
+	 * the 1.54 V boundary while it is on. */
+	if (!enabled)
+		return regulator_set_voltage_sel_regmap(rdev, sel);
 
 	ret = axp318_threshold_check(rdev, sel);
+	if (ret != -EBUSY) {
+		if (ret < 0)
+			return ret;
+
+		return regulator_set_voltage_sel_regmap(rdev, sel);
+	}
+
+	ret = regulator_disable_regmap(rdev);
 	if (ret < 0)
 		return ret;
 
-	return regulator_set_voltage_sel_regmap(rdev, sel);
+	ret = regulator_set_voltage_sel_regmap(rdev, sel);
+	if (ret < 0) {
+		regulator_enable_regmap(rdev);
+		return ret;
+	}
+
+	return regulator_enable_regmap(rdev);
 }
 
 static const struct regulator_ops axp20x_ops_fixed = {
